docker= is a platform that allows you to run containers. Which are OS specific software that you can run.
ECR/Elastic Container Registry: store container images
infrastructure->host OS-> Docker deamon-> container
EKS/Elastic kubernetes service
AWS fargate: own serveless contain platform
ECS/Elastic container service
ECS/Elastic container service
-------------------------------
launch ECS tasks on ECS cluster= docker container on AWS
ECS cluster-> EC2 instance-> ECS Agent-> ECS task-> docker container
Fargate launch type: no provisioning of the infrastructure. Increase number of tasks if you want to create more containers
ECSTask Role: allow each task to have a specific role so you can use different roles for each ECS service.
for load balancing: users->application load balancer-> cluster -> ec2 instances with ECS task inside
for EFS: EFS mounts on ECS cluster which has the EC2 instance/Fargate where the containers are inside.

ECS service auto scaling via AWS application auto scaling 
      -> ECS service average CPU utilization
      -> ECS service average memory usage
      -> ALB request count per target

Target tracking: scaling based on target value from a specific cloudwatch metric
step scaling: based on cloudwatch alarm
scheduled scaling: scale base on data/time
Auto scaling for group: based on CPU utilization, add EC2 instance over time
ECS cluster capacity provider: automatically provisioning of infrastructure for your ECS tasks. Capacity provider paired with an auto scaling group.

